<title>CHILE: Chile's Escondida Feb copper output falls.</title>
<headline>Chile's Escondida Feb copper output falls.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's Minera Escondida Limitada reported the following copper and gold production figures for February.</p>
<p>    COPPER (tonnes)	    Feb 97     Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p> Copper in concentrates	58,776     62,907	62,977</p>
<p> Copper cathodes		  5,019	5,501	 2,904</p>
<p> Total			     63,795     68,408	65,881</p>
<p>				  Jan-Feb 1997	    Jan-Feb 1996</p>
<p> Total			    132,204		    116,244</p>
<p> GOLD(ounces)		    Feb 97     Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p>				     11,899     12,138	16,882</p>
<p>NOTE: Minera Escondida is owned by Broken Hill Proprietary and RTZ Corp plc.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
